SESSION DESCRIPTION:  The National Security Agency in Washington has developed 
a prototype version of a security-enhanced Linux system. The prototype 
includes enhancements to Linux that provide new, stronger protection against 
tampering and bypassing of application security mechanisms, with greater 
limits on the damage that can be caused by malicious or flawed applications. 
SELinux is an ideal and secure operating system for government and big 
business. The principals have worked on SELinux under a DARPA/Air Force 
contract at The George Washington University's Cyber Security Policy and 
Research Institute. eGovOS.org is a consortium of university-based Open 
Source development centers around the country for the research and 
development of a secure Linux operating system. eGovOS is also getting a 
generic Linux distribution certified under the NIAP Common Criteria 
Evaluation and Validation Scheme, incorporating lessons learned from NSA's 
SELinux program. 
TARGET AUDIENCE:  government officials, security officials, general Linux 
users

